# Versioning and release

Release identity is `vx.y.z`. Stored version fields omit the leading `v` and use `x.y.z`. The Git tag and the version commit use `vx.y.z`.

## Increment

- New feature: increase `y` by 1 and reset `z` to 0.
- Fix or improvement to an existing feature: increase `z` by 1.
- Both a new feature and fixes: use the new-feature increment.
- Classify from the completed code, not from commit-message wording alone.
- If no new styles were created, do not increase the version. JavaScript, PHP, config, and docs changes are not enough. Do not edit styles only to justify a bump.
- If it is unclear whether the work is a feature or a fix, or whether the style condition was met, stop. Do not guess.

## Authoritative version

The plugin header `Version` in `nomreh.php` is the only stored software version. At runtime `get_plugin_data()` copies it into `NOMREH_PLUGIN_VERSION`. Do not add a second hardcoded copy of that number.

These are not the software version. Change them only when their own behavior changes:

- `NOMREH_DB_VERSION` — database schema marker. Compared with the `_nomreh_login_db_version` option before tables are created.
- `NOMREH_CRON_VERSION` — cron schedule marker. Compared with the `_nomreh_login_cron_version` option before events are rescheduled.
- `NOMREH_DEVELOPMENT` — when `true`, OTP is returned in the response and rate limiting is skipped. Production uploads require `false`.
- Composer metadata under `vendor/composer/` (`dev-main`). It is not read as the plugin version.

## Files to update for a release

Update only these when the version increases. They must all show the same `x.y.z`:

| File | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `nomreh.php` header `Version` | Source of truth. Becomes `NOMREH_PLUGIN_VERSION`, the installed version the update checker compares, and the admin asset cache key. |
| `readme.txt` `Stable tag` | Readme metadata. Must match the header. |
| `readme.txt` `== Changelog ==` and `== Upgrade Notice ==` | Newest section for the release. |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | Newest `## x.y.z` section for the same release. |

The version commit contains only those files. Commit message: `chore(release): vX.Y.Z`. Annotated tag on that commit: `vX.Y.Z` with message `vX.Y.Z`. Do not move, overwrite, or delete an existing tag. Do not push unless asked.

The update checker (`plugin_update_check()` in `nomreh.php`) points at `https://github.com/wproad/nomreh` on branch `main`. For `main` it prefers the latest GitHub Release, then the highest semver tag (a leading `v` is stripped), then the branch itself. The tag name and the header must be the same release.

## New styles

A version increase is allowed only when work since the last release tag (the last version bump, when that commit is the tag) includes newly created styles.

Compare both uncommitted changes and commits after that tag.

Qualifies:

- A new plugin-authored stylesheet under `assets/css/`.
- A material content change to `assets/css/public.css` or `assets/css/admin.css`.

Does not qualify:

- No diff in those stylesheets.
- Whitespace, formatting, or comment-only edits to an existing stylesheet.
- Changes limited to `assets/css/toastify.css` (third-party).
- Inline CSS from Settings → Styles (`nomreh_custom_styles` and the color/radius options). That CSS is stored in options and is not a shipped stylesheet.
- JavaScript, PHP, config, or docs only.

## Asset cache

There is no build manifest and no separate dev/prod asset pipeline. The same enqueue code runs in every environment.

- Public `assets/css/public.css`, `assets/css/toastify.css`, `assets/js/public.js`, and `assets/js/toastify.js`: the `ver` query argument is the file's `filemtime` when the file is readable, otherwise `NOMREH_PLUGIN_VERSION`. Editing those files busts the browser cache without a version bump.
- Admin `assets/css/admin.css` and `assets/js/admin.js`: the `ver` query argument is `NOMREH_PLUGIN_VERSION`. A plugin version bump is what invalidates those URLs.
- `NOMREH_DEVELOPMENT` does not change asset URLs.

## Production preparation

This plugin has no `package.json`, bundler, or compile step. `assets/css` and `assets/js` are the files that ship. `composer.json` has no requirements; `vendor/autoload.php` is already committed.

Before upload, confirm:

- Header, `Stable tag`, `CHANGELOG.md`, and the Git tag agree.
- `NOMREH_DEVELOPMENT` is `false`.
- `php -l nomreh.php` passes.
- `git status` shows no unintended files.
- Public assets still take their `ver` from `filemtime`, and admin assets still take it from `NOMREH_PLUGIN_VERSION`.

Do not regenerate `vendor/` or edit unrelated files as part of a release. There is no production build command to run.

## Stop the release when

- The style condition above is not met, or it is ambiguous.
- The working tree has changes that are not the version files (commit or clean those first; do not stash, reset, or mix them into the release commit).
- Header, `Stable tag`, and changelog disagree.
- `php -l` fails.
- The tag `vX.Y.Z` already exists.
- `NOMREH_DEVELOPMENT` is `true`.
- A version bump would also require a schema or cron change that was not made (`NOMREH_DB_VERSION` / `NOMREH_CRON_VERSION`).
